        "original_id": "fb7d5119-bce7-5740-b324-ba3d9a843bff",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Jonny Craig, Pete Doherty, Carl Barât\n- Bands and Projects: Dance Gavin Dance, Emarosa, Ghost Runner on Third, Slaves, westerHALTS, the Libertines, Babyshambles, Peter Doherty and the Puta Madres\n- Works: The Greatest of All Lost Arts, “Last of the English Roses”, “Pueblo Cicada”\n\nFacts:\n- Pete Doherty formed the Libertines with Carl Barât in 1997.\n- Jonathan Monroe \"Jonny\" Craig was born on March 26, 1986, and is a Canadian-American singer and songwriter.\n- Pete Doherty is best known as co-frontman of the Libertines.\n- Pete Doherty's other musical projects include the indie band Babyshambles and Peter Doherty and the Puta Madres.\n- “Last of the English Roses” is Peter Doherty's debut solo single.\n- Jonny Craig has been the lead vocalist for Dance Gavin Dance, Emarosa, Ghost Runner on Third, Slaves, and westerHALTS.\n- The album The Greatest of All Lost Arts contains 11 tracks.\n- Jonny Craig provided guest vocals on “Pueblo Cicada” on The Greatest of All Lost Arts.",
